sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
By default, declared width can exclude padding and border. `border-box` makes those parts count inside the declared box size.

```css
*, *::before, *::after {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
```

**Line by line:** `*` selects every element. The pseudo-elements are included too. `box-sizing: border-box` makes padding and border part of the element's declared width and height.

The portfolio image should scale down when space is narrow without being stretched taller.

```css
img {
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}
```

**Line by line:** `max-width: 100%` prevents the image from becoming wider than its container. `height: auto` preserves the image's natural aspect ratio.

A page can remain flexible while avoiding extremely long lines.

```css
main {
  width: 90%;
  max-width: 64rem;
}
```

**Line by line:** `width: 90%` lets main respond to available space. `max-width: 64rem` stops it from growing indefinitely. The earlier margin rule continues to center it.

